## What Problem This Solves

Gateway startup runs installation probes even when automatic update checks are disabled. These unnecessary Git/npm/pnpm commands can trigger the macOS Command Line Tools dialog and add startup work.

Fixes #158099. Supersedes #158119, thanks @ruel225 for the original repair and @Card4Philippe for confirming the remaining package-manager probes.

## User Impact

With `update.checkOnStart: false` or `OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1`, startup leaves installation discovery idle. With checks enabled, the first scheduled check discovers the installation. Explicit update/status requests still discover on demand and share the lifecycle's prepared installation facts.

No configuration, CLI, dependency, schema, or data migration changes. This takes effect when the candidate Gateway starts; it does not change the installed updater or rollback behavior.

## Why This Change Was Made

The Gateway post-attach adapter eagerly called `initialize()` before the scheduled update owner could apply its existing opt-out policy. Remove that competing entry point and its initialization bookkeeping. The scheduled owner already gates discovery, reports failures, and shares installation facts with explicit requests. Lifecycle cancellation continues to join admitted discovery.

Simplification: production **+0/-14 (net -14)**; tests **+74/-72 (net +2)**; docs **+4/-0**. Removed the obsolete eager-initialization test branches while retaining factory shutdown coverage and the real lifecycle's early-request/cancellation coverage. Added a process-boundary regression with the actual Gateway update owner.

