## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: independent system-agent tasks can fail with a superseded-runtime error when they wait in the queue while the calling runtime is replaced.

## User Impact

This is internal queue-owner hardening, with no newly demonstrated user-visible outage through normal delegation: ordinary delegate-tool ingress already exits these scopes. Independent queued tasks select current runtime facts without dropping the caller's identity or approval fences. No configuration change or migration is required.

## Why This Change Was Made

The existing system-agent queue now exits the ambient prepared-model and plugin-generation selection scopes before entering its task lock. The caller's authority scope and the resumed parent's original runtime scope remain intact. This reuses the existing scope-exit helpers; no second admission owner, new state, configuration, or permissions are introduced.

Related context: #157801 (selected helper-inference ownership, closed) and #159715 (merged follow-up-drain isolation). This patch targets the separate `runSystemAgentGatewayTask` queue owner.

